# Private company context — MUST NOT be published.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC (github.com/Bhaveshmeghwal21/pawaac-website), and
# PAWAAC_CONTEXT.md is an internal reference file, not site content. It records
# investor identity and contact, current fundraising status and the fund
# utilisation plan, cloud credit balances and a rejected application, the
# internal judgement that full L5 autonomy is not achievable in the current
# runway, named self-identified engineering weaknesses, an unresolved strategic
# question framed as shaping the investor narrative, and the framing chosen for
# a specific prospective police client. None of that should be readable by
# competitors, prospects or the press.
#
# It has never been committed, so ignoring it here is sufficient — no history
# rewrite is needed. CLAUDE.md still references it with `@PAWAAC_CONTEXT.md`,
# which is deliberate: the import simply no-ops in a clone that does not have
# the file, and it documents the intended local setup.
/PAWAAC_CONTEXT.md

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# design-sync (claude.ai/design import) — tooling scratch + generated output.
#
# Widened from three carve-outs to the whole directory. Nothing under src/
# imports anything from it and `next build` succeeds with it untracked, so it is
# not part of the app. The narrower rules left ~19 generated files staged for
# commit: hashed next/font .woff2 subsets, compiled CSS, and duplicate copies of
# components that already live in src/components/ui — the duplicates are the
# real reason to exclude it, since they go stale silently.
/.ds-sync/
/ds-bundle/
/.design-sync/

# Claude Code — share launch.json and settings.json (project dev-server config
# and permissions), keep per-developer overrides local.
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/*.local.json

# Unused sourced-but-unwired image — a candidate infrastructure sector photo
# generated during this session's sector re-sourcing work, superseded by the
# disaster-response tile before it was ever referenced in code (see
# HomeDeploymentsPreview.tsx header). Never committed, so ignoring is
# sufficient. Not the same as sector-defense-v2.jpg or
# sector-disaster-response.jpg, which ARE wired into the live sector tiles
# and must stay tracked.
/public/images/sector-infrastructure-v2.jpg
